      "interpretation": "Reject timeframe unequal to original before validating dirty timestamp. Raise ValueError for changed analysis timeframe. Require datetime instance, subclasses accepted; negate predicate. Raise TypeError for invalid dirty event. Visit old and new main timestamp sequences in that order. Containing candidate index is upper bound of original dirty event minus1, for each sequence independently. Only nonnegative index and dirty event strictly before main start+original timeframe rewind; equality at end excluded; addition is timestamp duration. Frontier min with containing main start; both histories may contribute.",
